WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.173
Tracing agents.

2
00:00:01.453 --> 00:00:04.739
Agents make tracing essential rather than nice to have.

3
00:00:05.019 --> 00:00:20.379
The semantic conventions model an agent run as an invoke_agent span whose children are chat spans for model calls and execute_tool spans for tool calls, and the OpenTelemetry team’s 2026 walkthrough shows exactly that tree.

4
00:00:20.659 --> 00:00:23.752
Three agent questions become easy once you have it.

5
00:00:24.032 --> 00:00:28.960
How many iterations did the loop take, and is that number creeping up release over release?

6
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:33.720
Which tool fails or times out most, and does the agent recover or spiral?

7
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:43.877
Where did the context grow: a trace with per-call input tokens shows the moment a large tool result entered the conversation and every later call paid for it.

8
00:00:44.157 --> 00:00:47.016
Record tool spans even for tools that “can’t fail.

9
00:00:47.296 --> 00:00:58.453
” An agent that called the same search tool eight times with slightly different queries is a prompt or tool-description problem, and it looks like nothing at all in a dashboard of model calls alone.
